WEBVTT

00:04.960 --> 00:08.020
I'll have you pay all the back rent.

00:09.380 --> 00:11.900
One, ten, hundred, thousand...

00:12.280 --> 00:13.710
Lots!

00:13.710 --> 00:14.910
So much?

00:15.200 --> 00:17.350
That's how much you've racked up.

00:18.070 --> 00:19.810
How about we get rid of a zero?

00:19.810 --> 00:21.350
Why would we?!

00:21.350 --> 00:24.420
Why not <i>add</i> a zero instead, then?

00:24.710 --> 00:25.740
Add?

00:25.740 --> 00:26.970
Preposterous!

00:26.970 --> 00:29.170
Would that even help anyone?

00:29.170 --> 00:30.050
It would.

00:30.720 --> 00:31.920
I could fix the bathroom.

00:32.500 --> 00:33.920
You can't tell immediately,

00:34.190 --> 00:37.550
but the Otowa bathroom is
in critical condition.

00:37.770 --> 00:40.970
We could save on water and
heating if we fixed it.

00:40.970 --> 00:44.940
1,500 yen a year... Maybe even 2,000!

00:45.290 --> 00:47.780
We could maybe even renovate it.

00:47.780 --> 00:49.650
Like, have a huge tub

00:50.010 --> 00:52.190
with a merleopon in it.

00:54.100 --> 00:56.110
Nah, I'm not actually hoping for that much.

00:56.110 --> 00:58.740
Just pay the rent, and I'll be happy.

00:59.400 --> 01:01.440
They got away again!

01:02.760 --> 01:04.300
A merleopon, huh?

01:04.300 --> 01:07.000
Kanae seemed pretty happy
about that thought.

01:07.570 --> 01:08.920
Want to try working?

01:09.210 --> 01:11.810
Want to try making an extra zero?

01:12.790 --> 01:14.660
For the merleopon!

02:47.290 --> 02:50.270
Huh? Beethoven and Mozart are?

02:50.590 --> 02:52.290
Out of our way, uniform!

02:51.150 --> 02:55.770
16: "Work! Beethes Motes"

02:52.290 --> 02:54.860
I told you, "staff only!"

02:54.860 --> 02:57.610
We <i>are</i> staff, I swear!

02:57.610 --> 02:59.230
What do you want?

02:59.850 --> 03:01.180
We're here to work.

03:01.180 --> 03:02.350
We've got enough people.

03:02.350 --> 03:05.100
They told us to become idols before.

03:05.100 --> 03:08.330
You threw a tantrum because you didn't
want to, and you made a huge mess.

03:09.220 --> 03:12.520
We're offering to pull ourselves
together and work for you.

03:12.520 --> 03:14.360
Where do you find the nerve?

03:14.360 --> 03:16.600
Enough lecturing, just let us work.

03:16.600 --> 03:18.510
We need to make money right now.

03:18.950 --> 03:20.410
Shall I call the police?

03:22.710 --> 03:26.060
I know of a way better place to work.

03:27.510 --> 03:29.480
Hayama Music Classes

03:29.480 --> 03:33.690
Boobies!

03:34.870 --> 03:35.900
Enough!

03:36.120 --> 03:37.070
Why?

03:37.070 --> 03:40.050
You're violating a beautiful melody!

03:40.050 --> 03:41.410
Absolutely disgusting!

03:41.410 --> 03:42.360
How rude.

03:42.790 --> 03:43.910
I'm not talking to you.

03:43.910 --> 03:46.260
I'm talking to this out-of-tune piano.

03:46.260 --> 03:47.530
Call a tuner!

03:47.530 --> 03:49.900
It's close enough to be a matter of taste.

03:49.900 --> 03:51.040
That's unacceptable to me.

03:51.450 --> 03:54.920
That's what's killing my inspiration!

03:55.170 --> 03:56.840
Call a tuner!

03:57.110 --> 03:58.730
You're so spoiled Lu-kun.

03:58.730 --> 03:59.980
Enough!

03:59.980 --> 04:01.340
Ow!

04:01.340 --> 04:04.710
You're too sloppy.

04:03.230 --> 04:06.940
I'm singing my boobies
song! Don't get in my way!

04:06.940 --> 04:10.160
They were introduced to us
through a company we work with.

04:11.560 --> 04:17.310
Hayama Music Classes
 Students Wanted

04:11.970 --> 04:14.210
We, here at Hayama Music Classes,

04:14.210 --> 04:17.310
strive to teach each and every
student the beauty of music,

04:17.310 --> 04:19.710
and to nurture the development

04:19.710 --> 04:22.650
of social skills and cooperation.

04:22.870 --> 04:24.660
So, how much can I make?

04:24.660 --> 04:26.170
We can start right away.

04:26.170 --> 04:29.510
I'm sorry. It may be difficult
to hire you as instructors.

04:30.140 --> 04:31.910
Why? We're geniuses!

04:31.910 --> 04:34.640
What more can you ask for
than genius instructors?

04:34.640 --> 04:37.170
I fully understand that you're geniuses.

04:37.170 --> 04:38.670
But your characters are a bit...

04:38.970 --> 04:40.310
A bit what?

04:40.310 --> 04:41.840
Your characters are a bit...

04:41.840 --> 04:43.990
What? Just say it.

04:43.990 --> 04:47.770
The way you <i>still</i> can't figure it
out, your characters are a bit...

04:48.460 --> 04:49.940
Music or character?

04:50.240 --> 04:52.400
Which is more important?

04:52.400 --> 04:54.710
And what do you mean by character?

04:55.010 --> 04:57.430
Inspiration and the pinnacle thereof.

04:57.430 --> 05:00.320
I have never failed to make
an effort to reach the top.

05:00.810 --> 05:03.440
But I've never thought about my character.

05:03.670 --> 05:04.820
I don't even care.

05:05.140 --> 05:06.790
Indeed! I feel no passion!

05:06.790 --> 05:08.910
I feel neither passion nor inspiration

05:08.910 --> 05:11.320
for a cryptic word like "character."

05:11.320 --> 05:13.240
What's a good job?

05:13.240 --> 05:17.040
A fun, easy job that'll make a lot of money.

05:17.040 --> 05:17.770
Huh?

05:18.480 --> 05:20.570
What're you guys doing here?

05:20.570 --> 05:21.500
Boy.

05:21.890 --> 05:23.560
Know any good jobs?

05:23.560 --> 05:25.140
You're going to work?

05:25.140 --> 05:26.210
We want...

05:26.210 --> 05:27.790
...an extra zero.

05:27.790 --> 05:29.530
All that rent, huh?

05:29.530 --> 05:30.390
No.

05:30.730 --> 05:32.130
Merleopon!

05:32.130 --> 05:33.020
No fountain way!

05:33.020 --> 05:34.520
Yes fountain way!

05:34.750 --> 05:35.680
No fountain way!

05:40.090 --> 05:42.220
You guys are hilarious.

05:46.040 --> 05:47.570
I don't know what you're talking about,

05:47.570 --> 05:50.620
but you can get some want ads
at the convenience store for free.

05:50.620 --> 05:51.530
Work
Job Listings
Take one free

05:52.620 --> 05:55.370
Easy work!
Good income!! High wages!!
Over 1,500 yen per hour!

05:52.940 --> 05:55.370
"High income, over 1,500 yen per hour."

05:55.370 --> 05:57.310
More zeroes!

05:57.610 --> 05:58.480
How about this one?

05:58.480 --> 06:00.920
"High income. 30,000
yen minimum per day guaranteed"

06:00.920 --> 06:01.920
A little more!

06:01.920 --> 06:03.430
That's the best one.

06:03.430 --> 06:04.550
Let's go with that, then.

06:04.550 --> 06:07.050
Jobs GO

06:04.820 --> 06:07.050
Let's see... "Give us a call!"

06:07.050 --> 06:07.990
Got it.

06:08.830 --> 06:09.590
Lend me your phone!

06:09.590 --> 06:24.110
Oden

06:10.130 --> 06:10.930
What?

06:10.930 --> 06:12.390
Lend me your phone!

06:12.390 --> 06:16.000
I'm sorry, we don't do things like that.

06:16.000 --> 06:19.250
Then what do we do?!

06:19.250 --> 06:19.830
Here!

06:19.830 --> 06:23.380
It says right here, to call
them if we want to work.

06:24.310 --> 06:26.660
Are you satisfied? Now lend me your phone!

06:27.290 --> 06:29.200
I'm pretty sure this is for women.

06:29.200 --> 06:30.200
What?!

06:30.200 --> 06:32.790
Why?! Girls only? Why?!

06:32.790 --> 06:35.430
We need to work!

06:35.430 --> 06:36.080
Uh...

06:36.080 --> 06:39.580
Jobs!
Employees Wanted!!

06:36.620 --> 06:38.630
Do you want to work here?

06:39.620 --> 06:40.580
Ludwig van Beethoven

06:40.620 --> 06:41.580
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart

06:41.820 --> 06:44.170
'kay, you fill up the drinks.

06:44.170 --> 06:45.480
You work the deep fryer.

06:45.480 --> 06:46.090
Yes, ma'am!

06:52.770 --> 06:54.120
The hell are you doing?

06:54.120 --> 06:55.570
I scared him.

07:01.070 --> 07:02.400
Why are you frying it again?!

07:02.700 --> 07:03.890
Experimenting.

07:03.890 --> 07:05.650
I shall never be satisfied
with the status quo.

07:05.650 --> 07:08.460
I am pursuing the next stage in deep frying.

07:10.890 --> 07:13.590
Dude, you know this is work, right?

07:13.590 --> 07:15.650
Yeah, we're just part-timers,

07:15.650 --> 07:17.750
but do it right.

07:19.710 --> 07:22.330
Don't you have anything to say?
You have mouths, don't you?

07:22.330 --> 07:23.630
I'm sorry.

07:23.630 --> 07:25.460
Seriously, get a grip.

07:25.730 --> 07:28.170
You're both grown-ups.

07:28.420 --> 07:29.380
Strawberry Milk

07:29.710 --> 07:30.720
Damn it...

07:31.840 --> 07:34.940
To think that there could be
a girl fiercer than Kanae...

07:34.940 --> 07:37.330
I'm trying so hard!

07:36.260 --> 07:37.760
Don't cry, Wolf!

07:37.760 --> 07:41.270
It's not like I don't want to
take it seriously, either.

07:41.270 --> 07:44.190
But I can't take it seriously
if it isn't fun.

07:44.190 --> 07:47.120
It's not that I don't, it's that I <i>can't</i>.

07:47.120 --> 07:49.650
I don't like doing things that
don't interest me, either.

07:50.250 --> 07:52.350
But we have no choice.

07:52.350 --> 07:53.590
We need money.

07:54.340 --> 07:56.370
For the merleopon!

07:59.350 --> 08:02.010
Okay, today's pay, please.

08:00.910 --> 08:02.010
Please.

08:00.910 --> 08:16.100
Oden

08:02.010 --> 08:05.180
No, it's not daily.

08:05.180 --> 08:07.440
Your salary's in a month.

08:07.440 --> 08:08.460
A month?!

08:08.460 --> 08:10.310
How much do we get?

08:10.310 --> 08:12.600
We have a good hourly wage, so if you

08:12.600 --> 08:15.020
come for all your shifts, you'll each get...

08:15.020 --> 08:16.100
Something like that.

08:17.880 --> 08:19.020
Farewell!

08:22.370 --> 08:23.630
Another zero...

08:23.630 --> 08:25.650
If only there was one more zero.

08:25.990 --> 08:28.150
You may call it common sense,

08:28.150 --> 08:30.310
but I won't accept it.

08:30.310 --> 08:31.010
No.

08:31.010 --> 08:33.570
Being strapped to common sense will not

08:33.790 --> 08:36.230
allow us to reach the heights of our ideals!

08:36.230 --> 08:38.070
Do we have to give up?

08:38.070 --> 08:39.590
No! We will find it!

08:39.590 --> 08:41.710
Our ideal job!

08:41.710 --> 08:43.500
A job that'll make us a lot of money!

08:43.800 --> 08:46.870
What? Are you guys looking for money?

08:47.540 --> 08:48.880
I have good work—

08:51.030 --> 08:52.880
Yes!

08:53.820 --> 08:57.140
And so we found new work.

08:57.510 --> 09:00.260
But it didn't meet our ideals,

09:00.260 --> 09:02.470
so we searched onward.

09:03.100 --> 09:04.440
We came closer to our ideal work...

09:04.950 --> 09:05.890
And fell further away...

09:06.280 --> 09:07.400
And we continued

09:07.810 --> 09:10.670
our search for ideal work.

09:11.120 --> 09:12.650
Money!

09:13.450 --> 09:14.980
And finally...

09:16.040 --> 09:19.830
Think of all the hell we've been
through to get this far, Motes-yan.

09:20.470 --> 09:24.030
This is nothing, Beethes-han.

09:24.030 --> 09:25.790
I'm not done yet.

09:26.030 --> 09:28.820
Aye, money makes money.

09:28.820 --> 09:31.470
Money gets lonely, you know.

09:31.470 --> 09:33.410
Hardy har har har.

09:35.260 --> 09:37.090
This doesn't seem right, does it?

09:37.090 --> 09:39.640
What were we trying to accomplish again?

09:41.500 --> 09:43.600
Get off your high horse, punks!

09:43.600 --> 09:47.060
Money

09:43.880 --> 09:47.070
I dare you to get on the bad side
of the city's shadow empire.

09:45.850 --> 09:47.810
Mujiiku

09:47.070 --> 09:48.850
I'll make mincemeat of you!

09:49.090 --> 09:52.020
So the last thing we did was <i>that</i>...

09:52.280 --> 09:55.870
Before that, we did that, and
the first thing we did...

09:55.870 --> 09:56.450
The convenience store!

09:56.710 --> 09:57.860
That's it, the convenience store!

09:57.860 --> 10:01.100
Why did we even decide to
work in the first place?

10:01.100 --> 10:03.490
Well, because... The, uh...

10:03.490 --> 10:04.300
M...

10:04.300 --> 10:05.580
M...

10:05.870 --> 10:07.770
Ma...

10:07.770 --> 10:09.630
They think they're being funny.

10:09.630 --> 10:11.000
Get ready to attack!

10:13.540 --> 10:14.980
Get 'em!

10:14.980 --> 10:15.880
Shut up!

10:16.230 --> 10:19.270
Musik!

10:24.620 --> 10:27.340
We almost got derailed.

10:27.340 --> 10:30.000
Yeah. Never forget your true purpose.

10:30.000 --> 10:32.520
It's not money that we seek.

10:34.040 --> 10:35.520
It's the merleopon!

10:42.970 --> 10:44.950
I fled from the

10:45.340 --> 10:47.500
clamorous city on a small train.

10:47.890 --> 10:50.120
Far, far away.

10:50.860 --> 10:52.380
Beautiful scenery.

10:52.900 --> 10:54.250
Strangers.

10:54.820 --> 10:57.420
Yes, this is heaven on Earth.

10:57.850 --> 11:00.100
It brings peace to my rowdy heart.

11:00.400 --> 11:03.040
The noise of the city is
but a distant memory.

11:03.040 --> 11:04.680
The world before me...

11:04.930 --> 11:05.930
Checking in!

11:06.280 --> 11:09.040
Hello, internet buddies!

11:09.040 --> 11:10.810
Outdoor Recluse Walker Choppin' here,

11:11.140 --> 11:14.320
bringing you along for another trek nao!

11:14.550 --> 11:17.400
That wretched mansion, the noisy rats...

11:17.400 --> 11:19.400
Everything that was tormenting
me is nothing but a phantom.

11:19.400 --> 11:22.870
I've been freed from that haunted
house, and now I have...

11:22.870 --> 11:24.710
Freedom!

11:26.370 --> 11:27.120
Choppin' TV

11:28.960 --> 11:31.340
That's Chopin-san, isn't it?

11:32.190 --> 11:33.820
Haunted house, huh?

11:33.820 --> 11:34.840
Huh.

11:36.090 --> 11:39.760
Outcluse Shut-out Walker "Choppin'" bringing you freedom!
Choppin' TV   184,110 plays

11:36.090 --> 11:39.760
Choppin' TV

11:36.500 --> 11:38.280
That's not his usual persona, is it?

11:38.280 --> 11:39.760
He's in his outcluse phase.

11:40.130 --> 11:41.020
His what?

11:41.320 --> 11:43.070
Cho-chan's a recluse,

11:43.070 --> 11:45.530
but a few times a year,
he goes out and doesn't come home.

11:45.530 --> 11:47.260
That's his outcluse phase.

11:47.640 --> 11:50.060
He's uploading videos when he's out.

11:51.520 --> 11:54.360
Dude, he's getting a crap ton of views.

11:54.580 --> 11:56.380
He's got a lot of fans, apparently.

11:58.360 --> 12:00.700
Would you cut that out already?

12:02.150 --> 12:03.650
Oh, you were, here Schu-san?

12:03.650 --> 12:05.890
Senpai, where art thou?

12:07.290 --> 12:09.160
He's not home?

12:09.160 --> 12:12.580
Oh yeah, I haven't seen Beethes
or Motes around lately.

12:12.850 --> 12:16.470
They were looking for work
last time I ran into them.

12:16.470 --> 12:18.630
They're finally willing to pay the rent!

12:18.630 --> 12:21.570
No, they were talking about,
like, a merleopon or something.

12:23.570 --> 12:24.440
Mer...?

12:24.440 --> 12:25.340
What's that?

12:25.700 --> 12:27.050
Merleopon.

12:27.050 --> 12:30.350
A leopon sculpture with the
scales and tail of a fish.

12:30.640 --> 12:32.690
What the? That's awesome!

12:33.220 --> 12:34.770
Ma... Ma...

12:35.440 --> 12:38.320
You're weird as hell,
though, laughing so hard.

12:36.710 --> 12:38.320
Ma... Ma...

12:38.320 --> 12:41.990
It seems to hit his peculiar giggle button.

12:42.240 --> 12:45.010
Huh, wait, why is it a merleopon, though?

12:45.010 --> 12:48.690
I said I wish we had a
merleopon in our bathroom.

12:48.690 --> 12:50.260
In the bathroom?!

12:51.810 --> 12:54.400
I was just kidding.
Did they take it seriously?

12:54.790 --> 12:55.850
I like it!

12:56.410 --> 12:57.980
A merleopon in the washroom!

12:57.980 --> 12:59.040
I really like it!

12:59.040 --> 13:00.800
I said I was kidding.

13:01.050 --> 13:02.500
Leave it to me.

13:09.340 --> 13:12.570
Why does everyone latch on to the
idea of a merleopon so much?

13:14.220 --> 13:16.830
Do you hear the tea leaves sing?

13:16.830 --> 13:18.810
It's a four-part chorus of antioxidants!

13:19.090 --> 13:22.660
A wave of soul-healing nature!

13:22.660 --> 13:24.080
And the three suns!

13:24.080 --> 13:25.140
What's the three suns, you ask?

13:25.140 --> 13:27.000
The sunny sun shining!

13:27.000 --> 13:29.120
Sunny sun, son!

13:29.950 --> 13:31.410
This is freedom!

13:31.630 --> 13:32.870
This is healing!

13:33.270 --> 13:36.560
There's no penny-pincher
here nagging me for rent.

13:36.560 --> 13:38.580
No annoying tool boy.

13:38.580 --> 13:42.270
No make-up monster who gets in my face
both physically and emotionally.

13:42.270 --> 13:44.190
No stubborn, argumentative fuzzhead!

13:44.190 --> 13:46.700
No long-haired, tactless pervert!

13:46.700 --> 13:47.380
No one!

13:47.760 --> 13:50.630
There's no one else in my world!

13:50.630 --> 13:53.890
Hey there, stranger, come
hither for some tea.

13:54.120 --> 13:56.900
Our tea is splendid!

13:56.900 --> 13:59.180
The locals are so kind.

13:59.480 --> 14:01.860
Thank you, man!

14:05.340 --> 14:06.360
What's the matter?

14:06.600 --> 14:08.460
Beethes! Motes! Why?

14:08.460 --> 14:10.570
Sorry, sorry, I'm sorry...

14:10.570 --> 14:12.580
Oh, don't say that.

14:12.890 --> 14:14.770
Take a sip.

14:19.500 --> 14:20.130
No!

14:20.130 --> 14:21.750
I'm not Chopin!

14:21.750 --> 14:24.270
I'm Outcluse Walker Choppin'!

14:24.270 --> 14:25.890
I don't know you one bit!

14:26.190 --> 14:28.110
We're total strangers!

14:28.110 --> 14:30.870
So obviously I wasn't talking
about you just now.

14:31.950 --> 14:33.640
Would you like some?

14:34.770 --> 14:36.550
You aren't Beethes and Motes?

14:37.660 --> 14:40.500
We're Benzo and Arukichi.

14:40.500 --> 14:43.190
We've worked on this tea farm all our lives.

14:43.440 --> 14:44.150
Liars!

14:44.150 --> 14:46.170
You're Beethes and Motes!

14:46.170 --> 14:48.200
Say what, now?

14:48.200 --> 14:49.360
Look carefully!

14:49.360 --> 14:50.930
It's me, Chopin!

14:50.930 --> 14:53.280
Come on! Look carefully!

14:50.930 --> 14:54.580
Spare us, traveler.

14:56.430 --> 14:57.660
She actually did it...

14:57.960 --> 14:59.170
And it's actually good.

14:59.170 --> 15:01.580
Did she just discover a new talent?

15:01.840 --> 15:02.740
No.

15:05.610 --> 15:08.430
It's not what I've envisioned!

15:08.430 --> 15:11.840
Love. There's not enough love!

15:13.740 --> 15:15.060
That's right.

15:15.060 --> 15:16.640
I'd completely forgotten.

15:16.640 --> 15:19.250
We were totally Arukichi and Benzo.

15:19.250 --> 15:21.850
S-So why are you all the way
up here in the mountains?

15:23.480 --> 15:25.030
We've been through a lot.

15:25.030 --> 15:27.790
We almost turned evil at one point.

15:27.790 --> 15:30.190
But we got out, and....

15:30.190 --> 15:34.740
We set out once again to
find high-paying work.

15:35.520 --> 15:37.740
Some jobs were dangerous.

15:38.400 --> 15:42.030
Some terrible jobs that
put us in mortal peril.

15:42.700 --> 15:44.450
You're exaggerating.

15:44.450 --> 15:45.960
Only a little bit.

15:45.960 --> 15:47.550
Okay, okay, so?

15:48.560 --> 15:49.950
Money, money, money...

15:50.250 --> 15:52.630
We became sick of our lives,

15:53.460 --> 15:56.210
and soon, we were dead inside.

15:57.200 --> 15:59.640
That's when we were taken up...

16:00.640 --> 16:02.390
By a huge eagle.

16:03.350 --> 16:05.810
And so began our journey of adventure.

16:07.200 --> 16:09.490
We faced trial after trial.

16:10.400 --> 16:12.630
We met some people, and we parted ways.

16:13.580 --> 16:14.740
At times, we fought.

16:14.990 --> 16:16.540
You fool!

16:16.540 --> 16:18.080
I cannot change my way of life!

16:18.080 --> 16:19.400
We're friends, aren't we?!

16:25.610 --> 16:27.340
Our friendship was made deeper.

16:28.490 --> 16:30.280
Alas, the two of us were

16:30.280 --> 16:32.800
struck down by a formidable adversary.

16:33.100 --> 16:34.920
Oh, my God!

16:37.760 --> 16:43.560
Tobacco

16:38.600 --> 16:40.930
Wolf's bullshit aside,

16:40.930 --> 16:43.560
things happened, and we ended up here.

16:43.560 --> 16:45.090
It's not bullshit.

16:45.390 --> 16:48.730
Benzo, Arukichi, have some lunch.

16:48.730 --> 16:50.940
Your friend, too.

16:54.740 --> 16:57.420
This place sure is paradise.

16:58.490 --> 17:00.370
Delicious food.

17:00.370 --> 17:01.780
And beautiful nature.

17:01.780 --> 17:03.510
Kind people.

17:04.420 --> 17:05.250
But...

17:06.060 --> 17:08.860
I feel like we're forgetting
something important.

17:09.470 --> 17:10.930
Come to think of it...

17:12.280 --> 17:13.930
Something important?

17:13.930 --> 17:16.140
Something we'd been pursuing.

17:16.470 --> 17:18.180
Not money...

17:18.450 --> 17:19.290
M...

17:19.900 --> 17:20.930
Mer...

17:21.170 --> 17:22.130
Mat...

17:22.430 --> 17:23.150
...cha?

17:23.750 --> 17:24.830
Nah, I'm kidding.

17:25.770 --> 17:27.170
Matcha!

17:27.610 --> 17:28.810
That's it!

17:29.170 --> 17:32.400
Behold! This is the land of the
tea leaves that are to

17:32.400 --> 17:34.900
become the matcha that we have longed for.

17:35.250 --> 17:36.440
Look over there!

17:36.440 --> 17:37.660
There are angels here, too.

17:38.040 --> 17:39.670
Benzo-san!

17:39.670 --> 17:41.160
Arukichi-san!

17:42.540 --> 17:43.680
Paradise!

17:43.680 --> 17:45.710
This is matcha paradise!

17:45.710 --> 17:48.930
Matcha! Matcha!

17:50.440 --> 17:51.400
So there you have it.

17:51.400 --> 17:54.080
Us two are going to live here
in this matcha paradise.

17:54.080 --> 17:56.060
You aren't coming back to Otowakan?

17:56.060 --> 17:57.090
We're abandoning our past!

17:57.400 --> 18:00.310
If this is Paradise, then that
makes that place Hell.

18:00.310 --> 18:01.490
Rent hell.

18:01.490 --> 18:03.940
We might come home if we get bored.

18:03.940 --> 18:05.680
Say hi to Kanae for me.

18:06.150 --> 18:09.020
Matcha! Matcha!

18:09.860 --> 18:10.730
So, yeah.

18:11.030 --> 18:12.300
I see.

18:12.300 --> 18:15.420
I'm not <i>asking</i> them to live here, of course.

18:15.420 --> 18:16.790
I-I see.

18:16.790 --> 18:17.750
Senpai...

18:18.050 --> 18:19.280
Are you there?

18:21.520 --> 18:22.870
Senpai!

18:22.870 --> 18:25.070
I'm coming for you!

18:25.370 --> 18:27.290
Does he know where they are?

18:27.710 --> 18:28.470
So...

18:29.000 --> 18:32.040
You don't have to live here, either.

18:32.040 --> 18:34.410
"Outcluse Walker," was it?

18:34.410 --> 18:35.210
Well...

18:35.210 --> 18:38.560
This place is haunted, yes?

18:38.560 --> 18:41.970
And I'm a penny-pincher, right?

18:43.750 --> 18:45.720
I have no idea what you're talking about.

18:46.880 --> 18:47.920
You sound pretty sure.

18:47.920 --> 18:48.860
I'm sure.

18:49.480 --> 18:51.980
Closed

18:50.330 --> 18:53.970
The seedlings aren't growing well this year.

18:53.970 --> 18:56.050
It's the abnormal weather.

18:56.050 --> 18:59.570
El Niño is hurting us all the
way up in these mountains.

19:00.120 --> 19:01.480
Oh, dear.

19:01.480 --> 19:04.450
How ever will we harvest good tea leaves?

19:05.050 --> 19:07.310
It's over for this place.

19:07.610 --> 19:09.180
This is our fate.

19:11.490 --> 19:14.380
We've finally come to paradise, but...

19:15.000 --> 19:17.510
We have no choice but to bring back

19:18.230 --> 19:20.220
the past we'd once abandoned.

19:20.740 --> 19:22.350
Cower before us!

19:22.720 --> 19:25.520
To save this land!

20:04.710 --> 20:06.180
It's a miracle!

20:06.180 --> 20:08.560
Was this an act of God?!

20:08.560 --> 20:10.060
Benzo! Arukichi!

20:10.420 --> 20:13.340
Let's harvest!
We're going to be busy!

20:13.340 --> 20:14.440
We are.

20:15.670 --> 20:16.710
You know,

20:17.230 --> 20:20.580
maybe this is what happiness is.

20:21.430 --> 20:25.400
Maybe we really should just live here.

20:25.700 --> 20:26.380
Yeah.

20:26.950 --> 20:29.120
I plan to be buried here.

20:30.120 --> 20:32.240
Me, too. That's my plan.

20:32.960 --> 20:36.570
Let's protect this matcha paradise
for the rest of our lives.

20:36.850 --> 20:37.600
Yeah.

20:41.590 --> 20:43.510
It's not much, but here's your pay.

20:43.840 --> 20:46.080
The harvest season is over.

20:46.410 --> 20:48.780
Be well. Have some fresh tea.

20:51.390 --> 20:53.690
Farewell!

20:57.250 --> 20:58.820
We're home!

20:59.830 --> 21:01.740
I thought you'd abandoned your pasts.

21:02.000 --> 21:03.980
We did, but we picked it back up.

21:03.980 --> 21:07.080
We got thrown out, now
that the season's over.

21:07.080 --> 21:08.350
Here you go, souvenir gift.

21:08.350 --> 21:10.270
Thank you.
Do you have rent?

21:10.270 --> 21:11.120
Nope.

21:11.450 --> 21:15.130
We spent it on our train fare home
and on food and other necessities.

21:15.130 --> 21:17.210
The unagi was so good.

21:17.210 --> 21:18.300
Damn it.

21:18.300 --> 21:19.630
Done!

21:20.400 --> 21:23.880
Oh, Liszt-san's been hooked
on merleopon carving.

21:25.380 --> 21:26.600
That's right.

21:26.600 --> 21:28.070
That was our objective.

21:28.070 --> 21:29.640
Not matcha.

21:30.690 --> 21:32.390
Merleopon!

21:34.770 --> 21:35.640
Behold.

21:35.980 --> 21:37.480
My masterpiece.

21:37.480 --> 21:39.580
The merleopon of love!

21:40.180 --> 21:42.530
I don't think this is right.

21:42.930 --> 21:44.970
Th-This is a mer...

21:44.970 --> 21:46.120
...leopon?

21:46.510 --> 21:48.450
N-No fountain way.

21:48.450 --> 21:50.750
It actually shoots water
from its mouth, too.

21:52.500 --> 21:54.020
Awesome!

21:54.320 --> 21:55.550
Merleopon.

21:55.850 --> 21:57.140
Merleopon?

21:58.330 --> 21:59.870
Merleopon?

22:00.990 --> 22:01.930
No, it's not.

22:02.750 --> 22:05.820
All right, let's take the
merleopon to the bathroom.

22:05.820 --> 22:06.880
Help me, guys.

22:06.880 --> 22:10.270
What? No way, that's not going to fit.

22:10.270 --> 22:13.550
We should shout "Mersshoi" when we carry it.

22:13.550 --> 22:13.900
What?

22:13.900 --> 22:15.320
Ready, and...

22:15.320 --> 22:18.290
Mersshoi! Mersshoi!

22:16.360 --> 22:18.290
Wait!

22:18.290 --> 22:21.230
Mersshoi! Mersshoi!

22:27.230 --> 22:28.940
We'll find him, believe me.

22:28.940 --> 22:31.690
My senpai knows <i>everyone</i>. Seriously.

22:31.690 --> 22:34.070
Senpai... Where art thou?

22:34.070 --> 22:35.760
Quit crying!

22:35.760 --> 22:36.960
You're a grown man.

22:37.180 --> 22:42.680
Senpai!

22:40.310 --> 22:42.680
Stop that. You're a grown man.

22:43.000 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

24:15.970 --> 24:26.650
Episode 17: Mandarins!
Mandarins! Fried Mandarins?!

24:16.790 --> 24:18.780
Have you heard of the
curse of the mandarins?

24:18.780 --> 24:20.840
Fear, fear the curse
of the mandarins.

24:20.840 --> 24:22.690
A stem shall grow on
the whorl of your hair,

24:22.690 --> 24:24.220
and your skin shall become
bumpy and orange.

24:24.220 --> 24:26.110
Try as you might to be
the star of the kotatsu,

24:26.110 --> 24:28.600
you'll be a round and stumpy
disaster, believe me.
